 for your job, the person who left it. Ask each of them the same three questions:"}</p><ul className={"custom-dots"} role={"list"}><li>{"What should I keep exactly as it is?"}</li><li>{"What is everyone here too polite to tell me?"}</li><li>{"If you had my job, what would you do first?"}</li></ul><blockquote className={"my-12 py-8 font-heading text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.35rem_+_1.4vw,2.5rem)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.015em] text-balance custom-article-pull"}><p>{"“The first hundred days are rarely lost to a bad decision. "}<em>{"They are lost to a full diary."}</em>{"”"}</p></blockquote><h2 id={"ec-ar-stop"}>{"Days 31–60: decide what to stop"}</h2><p>{"New leaders add. They add meetings to learn, reports to see, reviews to feel in control. By week six the diary has no white space and the team has learned that every decision goes through you."}</p><p>{"Make a list of everything that comes to your desk in a fortnight. Then give a third of it away, by name, in writing. One client of ours cancelled four standing meetings in a single afternoon. Nobody missed them."}</p><figure className={"my-10 p-[clamp(1.5rem,1rem_+_1.5vw,2.25rem)] rounded-28 bg-(--custom-card)"} aria-labelledby={"ec-ar-fig-title"}><figcaption id={"ec-ar-fig-title"} className={"mb-6 font-heading text-[1.5rem] leading-[1.2] custom-article-figure-title"}>{"What new executives had in place by day 90"}<span>{"The 2026 Leadership Pulse · 1,200 leaders, 14 countries"}</span></figcaption><dl className={"grid gap-4.5 custom-article-bars"}><div style={{"--custom-value": "38%"}}><dt>{"A written plan for their first ninety days"}</dt><dd className={"tabular-nums"}>{"38%"}</dd></div><div style={{"--custom-value": "46%"}}><dt>{"Goals agreed with their sponsor in month one"}</dt><dd className={"tabular-nums"}>{"46%"}</dd></div><div style={{"--custom-value": "57%"}}><dt>{"One-to-ones with every direct report"}</dt><dd className={"tabular-nums"}>{"57%"}</dd></div><div style={{"--custom-value": "29%"}}><dt>{"A coach or me